/-!
# The generic fibre of the strict henselisation of a local ring of a smooth curve

Let `A` be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field `K` and let `A → A^{sh}` be a strict
henselisation of `A`. The generic fibre of `Spec A^{sh} → Spec A` is `Spec (A^{sh} ⊗[A] K)`, and
this file identifies that ring: `A^{sh}` is again a discrete valuation ring, and
`A^{sh} ⊗[A] K` is its fraction field.

The reason is that `A^{sh} ⊗[A] K` is the localisation of `A^{sh}` at the image of the nonzero
elements of `A`, and a uniformiser `ϖ` of `A` stays a uniformiser of `A^{sh}`: the maximal ideal
of a henselisation is the extension of the maximal ideal of the base
(`IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.map_maximalIdeal`), so `𝔪_{A^{sh}}` is generated by the image of
`ϖ`. Every nonzero element of the discrete valuation ring `A^{sh}` is therefore a unit times a
power of that image, hence already invertible once the image of `ϖ` has been inverted; so
inverting the nonzero elements of `A` inverts all of them.

At a closed point `x` of a smooth curve `X` over a field the local ring `𝒪_{X, x}` is a discrete
valuation ring (`AlgebraicGeometry.IsCurve.isDiscreteValuationRing_stalk_of_isClosed`) with
fraction field the function field of `X`, so the statement applies there: the generic fibre
`Spec (𝒪^{sh}_{X, x} ⊗_{𝒪_{X, x}} K)` is the spectrum of the fraction field of the discrete
valuation ring `𝒪^{sh}_{X, x}`.

## Main results

* `IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.isFractionRing_tensorProduct_of_isDiscreteValuationRing`: **the
  generic fibre of a strict henselisation of a discrete valuation ring is the fraction field of
  that strict henselisation**, which is again a discrete valuation ring.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.IsCurve.isFractionRing_tensorProduct_functionField`: the same at a closed
  point of a smooth curve over a field, where the discrete valuation ring is the local ring of
  the curve and its fraction field is the function field.

## Implementation notes

The strict henselisation is an arbitrary model satisfying `IsLocalRing.IsHenselization A ksep
A^{sh}` for a separable closure `ksep` of the residue field of `A`, which is how the rest of this
library speaks about it; the henselisation that
`isDiscreteValuationRing_iff_henselizations` additionally needs is supplied by the chosen
`IsLocalRing.henselizationTower`. The residue closure `ksep` may live in its own universe; the
three rings `A`, `K` and `A^{sh}` share one, as they do in the geometric application, where all
three are rings of a scheme in `Scheme.{u}`.

The discrete valuation ring conclusions are stated in the shape
`∃ _ : IsDomain A^{sh}, IsDiscreteValuationRing A^{sh} ∧ _`, because `IsDiscreteValuationRing`
cannot be stated without an `IsDomain` instance; this is the shape in which
`isDiscreteValuationRing_iff_henselizations` already carries them. The `IsFractionRing` clause
does not depend on the `IsDomain` instance — it is a localisation statement — but it is what
makes the ring a *field*, so the three are stated together.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached: this is a component of the stalk computation of
[Stacks, Tag 03Q9] used by [Stacks, Tag 03RJ], not a tag of its own.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03Q9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03Q9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03RJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03RJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AP3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AP3)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory IsLocalRing

open scoped TensorProduct

universe u v

namespace IsLocalRing.IsHenselization

/-- **The generic fibre of a strict henselisation of a discrete valuation ring is the fraction
field of that strict henselisation.** Let `A` be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field
`K`, let `ksep` be a separable closure of the residue field of `A`, and let `Ash` be a strict
henselisation of `A` with residue field `ksep`. Then `Ash` is again a discrete valuation ring,
and the generic fibre `Ash ⊗[A] K` of `Spec Ash → Spec A` is its fraction field.

`Ash` is a discrete valuation ring by [Stacks, Tag 0AP3]. The tensor product is the localisation
of `Ash` at the image of the nonzero elements of `A`, and the image of a uniformiser of `A`
generates the maximal ideal of `Ash`, so it is a uniformiser there; every nonzero element of
`Ash` is a unit times a power of it, hence becomes invertible. -/
@[ega "IV 18.8.12" "(i), special case",
  ega "IV 18.8.8" "(iv), special case",
  sga "4 VIII 4.4" "special case"]
theorem isFractionRing_tensorProduct_of_isDiscreteValuationRing
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [IsDiscreteValuationRing A]
    (K : Type u) [Field K] [Algebra A K] [IsFractionRing A K]
    (Ash : Type u) [CommRing Ash] [IsLocalRing Ash] [Algebra A Ash]
    (ksep : Type v) [Field ksep] [Algebra (ResidueField A) ksep]
    [IsSepClosure (ResidueField A) ksep] [IsHenselization A ksep Ash] :
    ∃ _ : IsDomain Ash, IsDiscreteValuationRing Ash ∧ IsFractionRing Ash (Ash ⊗[A] K) := by
  obtain ⟨hdom, hdvr⟩ := (isDiscreteValuationRing_iff_henselizations A
    (henselizationTower A ksep).henselization Ash ksep).2.mp ⟨‹_›, ‹_›⟩
  refine ⟨hdom, hdvr, ?_⟩
  let := hdom
  let := hdvr
  obtain ⟨ϖ, hϖ⟩ := IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_irreducible A
  have hmax : maximalIdeal Ash = Ideal.span {algebraMap A Ash ϖ} := by
    rw [← IsHenselization.map_maximalIdeal (R := A) (L := ksep) (Rh := Ash),
      (IsDiscreteValuationRing.irreducible_iff_uniformizer ϖ).mp hϖ, Ideal.map_span,
      Set.image_singleton]
  have hirr : Irreducible (algebraMap A Ash ϖ) :=
    (IsDiscreteValuationRing.irreducible_iff_uniformizer _).mpr hmax
  have : IsLocalization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid Ash (nonZeroDivisors A)) (Ash ⊗[A] K) :=
    IsLocalization.tensor (S := Ash) K (nonZeroDivisors A)
  have hunit : IsUnit (algebraMap Ash (Ash ⊗[A] K) (algebraMap A Ash ϖ)) :=
    IsLocalization.map_units (M := Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid Ash (nonZeroDivisors A)) _
      ⟨_, ⟨ϖ, mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_ne_zero hϖ.ne_zero, rfl⟩⟩
  refine IsLocalization.of_le (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid Ash (nonZeroDivisors A)) _ ?_ ?_
  · rintro x ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩
    rw [mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_ne_zero]
    obtain ⟨n, u, rfl⟩ :=
      IsDiscreteValuationRing.eq_unit_mul_pow_irreducible (nonZeroDivisors.ne_zero ha) hϖ
    simp only [map_mul, map_pow]
    exact mul_ne_zero (u.isUnit.map (algebraMap A Ash)).ne_zero (pow_ne_zero _ hirr.ne_zero)
  · intro b hb
    obtain ⟨n, u, rfl⟩ :=
      IsDiscreteValuationRing.eq_unit_mul_pow_irreducible (nonZeroDivisors.ne_zero hb) hirr
    simpa using (u.isUnit.map (algebraMap Ash (Ash ⊗[A] K))).mul (hunit.pow n)

end IsLocalRing.IsHenselization

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.IsCurve

/-- **The generic fibre of the strict henselisation of a local ring of a smooth curve is the
fraction field of that discrete valuation ring.** Let `k` be a field, let `X` be a curve over `k`
which is smooth over `k`, let `x` be a closed point of `X`, and let `Ash` be a strict
henselisation of the local ring `𝒪_{X, x}`, with residue field a separable closure `ksep` of the
residue field at `x`. Then `Ash` is a discrete valuation ring and the generic fibre
`Ash ⊗_{𝒪_{X, x}} K` — the base change of `Ash` to the function field `K` of `X` — is its
fraction field.

The local ring of a smooth curve at a closed point is a discrete valuation ring, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsCurve.isDiscreteValuationRing_stalk_of_isClosed`, and the function field of
an integral scheme is the fraction field of each of its local rings; so this is
`IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.isFractionRing_tensorProduct_of_isDiscreteValuationRing` read at
`𝒪_{X, x}`. -/
@[ega "IV 18.8.12" "(i), special case", ega "IV 18.8.15" "special case"]
theorem isFractionRing_tensorProduct_functionField (k : Type u) [Field k] {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsCurve k f] [Smooth f] {x : X} (hx : IsClosed ({x} : Set X))
    (Ash : Type u) [CommRing Ash] [IsLocalRing Ash] [Algebra (X.presheaf.stalk x) Ash]
    (ksep : Type v) [Field ksep] [Algebra (ResidueField (X.presheaf.stalk x)) ksep]
    [IsSepClosure (ResidueField (X.presheaf.stalk x)) ksep]
    [IsHenselization (X.presheaf.stalk x) ksep Ash] :
    ∃ _ : IsDomain Ash, IsDiscreteValuationRing Ash ∧
      IsFractionRing Ash (Ash ⊗[X.presheaf.stalk x] X.functionField) :=
  let := isDiscreteValuationRing_stalk_of_isClosed k f hx
  IsHenselization.isFractionRing_tensorProduct_of_isDiscreteValuationRing
    (X.presheaf.stalk x) X.functionField Ash ksep

end AlgebraicGeometry.IsCurve

end
